      "candidate_id": "cand_002",
      "high_level_variant": "Ego follows its route into a mildly denser mixed-traffic area where a crossing vehicle from the side approaches and is detected and predicted, but ego continues forward and collides laterally without braking while planning still outputs unblocked waypoints and vehicle_cmd stays all zero.",
      "mutation_intent": "Shift the primary interacting actor to approach from a lateral direction while keeping the ego moving and preserving active perception/prediction and unblocked planning outputs alongside a zeroed vehicle_cmd stream. The lateral configuration explores whether the same command–status mismatch and unexplained collision arise when the nearby actor is not purely longitudinal, without changing the core root-cause pattern.",
      "expected_oracle": "collision",
      "modifications": {
        "weather_delta": {
          "rain": -5,
          "fog": 5,
          "wetness": 0,
          "puddle": 0
        },
        "actor_mutations": [
          {
            "actor_index": 3,
            "position_offset": {
              "x": -4.0,
              "y": 3.0
            },
            "speed_delta": 1.5
          },
          {
            "actor_index": 2,
            "position_offset": {
              "x": -2.0,
              "y": -3.0
            },
            "speed_delta": -2.0
          },
          {
            "actor_index": 0,
            "position_offset": {
              "x": -5.0,
              "y": -1.0
            },
            "speed_delta": 0.5
          },
          {
            "actor_index": 1,
            "position_offset": {
              "x": -1.0,
              "y": 2.0
            },
            "speed_delta": 0.0
          }
        ],
        "puddle_mutations": [],
        "mission_mutation": {
          "keep_original": false,
          "spawn_offset": {
            "x": 3.0,
            "y": -2.0
          },
          "destination_offset": {
            "x": -4.0,
            "y": 1.0
          }
        }
      },
      "pre_execution_validation_rules": [
        "Verify that actor_index 3’s adjusted pose and speed create a plausible lateral or diagonal path that intersects the ego lane within the simulation horizon, so that a potential side collision region exists.",
        "Confirm that the mission spawn and destination offsets still place ego on a continuous roadway path without invalid or off-road starts/ends.",
        "Ensure perception and prediction topics are active and configured to detect and track vehicles approaching from the sides, not just purely longitudinal traffic.",
        "Check planning still produces full final_waypoints with no preconfigured blocked segments or emergency-stop logic specific to cross-traffic in this map region.",
        "Confirm the controller and simulator configuration still allow vehicle_status to report ego motion even when vehicle_cmd fields may remain zero."
      ],
      "post_execution_validation_rules": [
        "Confirm oracle collision logs a collision between ego and a non-ego vehicle (preferably actor_index 3) near the end of the run.",
        "Verify ego velocity remains nonzero leading up to the collision and there is no significant increase in brake_cmd before impact.",
        "Check that perception/prediction topics report the laterally approaching vehicle with positions and predicted trajectories that intersect or closely approach the ego’s path in the seconds before the collision.",
        "Ensure final_waypoints remain present, with consistent counts and no blocked flags, throughout the pre-collision window, indicating planning did not explicitly mark the path as obstructed.",
        "Validate that vehicle_cmd accel_cmd, brake_cmd, steer_cmd, and target_speed stay effectively at zero while vehicle_status shows ongoing motion, reproducing the command–status mismatch.",
        "Inspect any planner summary metrics (e.g., closest-object-distance) to verify that they do not trigger a stop or blocked-plan condition even as the lateral actor nears the ego."
      ],
      "uncertainty": [
        "Changing the main interacting actor to a lateral vehicle may influence how perception and prediction represent the scene, so it remains uncertain whether the same misalignment between their outputs and planning/control will occur.",
        "The underlying cause of the zero vehicle_cmd despite ego motion is still ambiguous; this variant tests whether the phenomenon generalizes to cross-traffic, but does not identify which module is responsible if the pattern repeats."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

